## Source (verbatim, TeX of arXiv:2611.16719v1)
```text
Two objects attached to \(\ket\psi\) organize the analysis: the \emph{coefficient operator}, which maps each \(\ket{c_j}\) to \(x_j\ket{c_j}\), and the \emph{component Gram matrix},
\begin{equation}
\cX_\psi=\sum_jx_j\ketbra{c_j}{c_j^\perp},\quad G_\psi=X^\dagger SX,
\label{eq:Gpsi}
\end{equation}
with \(X=\diag(x)\), so that \(G_\psi\) is the Gram matrix of the components \(x_j\ket{c_j}\) of \(\ket\psi\) and carries the weights \(|x_j|^2\) on its diagonal; in coherence theory (\(S=\one\)) it is the diagonal matrix of the populations.
```
It checks the source’s $N=2,3$ optima, all 12,870 balanced signs, the two symbolic dual bounds and strict gap, and the rational certificate on 64 sampled and 64 constructed signed-coordinate bijections.
